POPEYE IN COLOR — download-only pending a Catalog of Copyright Entries check.
Owner decision, 2026-07-26.

WHY THIS PACK IS NOT PRELOADED
------------------------------
The PD-cartoons field guide (July 2026) describes the Technicolor two-reelers as
circulating on PD compilations "with a murkier claim — verify before commercial
use," and the starter-pack shortlist lists them under do-not-include PENDING
VERIFICATION. This pack's manifest basis (IA public-domain marks + documented
non-renewal) predates that research.

Nothing here says the pack is NOT public domain. All three source items are live
on the Internet Archive with PD marks — there is no takedown and no dispute on
record. The gap is documentary: NR (non-renewal) is a lead, not a clearance,
until someone reads the renewal volumes.

So the pack stays curated, stays in the catalog, and stays one tap away — it
just does not ride inside the App Store binary, where our name is on it most
directly and the exposure is least reversible. Removing it also brought the
preload bundle to ~348 MB, inside the D1 target, so the rights question and the
size dial pointed the same way.

TO CLEAR IT (≈1 hour of real work)
----------------------------------
Search the Catalog of Copyright Entries renewal volumes for 1963-1967 (28 years
after 1936/1937/1939 release) for:
  - Popeye the Sailor Meets Sindbad the Sailor (1936)
  - Popeye the Sailor Meets Ali Baba's Forty Thieves (1937)
  - Aladdin and His Wonderful Lamp (1939)
Watch for renewals filed under a RETITLED reissue, which is the standard trap.
The volumes are scanned and searchable on the Internet Archive and Google Books.
Cross-check Hurst's "Film Superlist".

If it clears: restore the PRELOAD marker and delete this file.
If it does not: remove the pack from packs/index.json and the repo.

Note the character/trademark position is separate and unchanged: the 1929
Thimble Theatre Popeye is public domain, King Features holds the trademark, and
the pack is never used in dumbTV marketing.
